      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T05:50:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For this particular one it seems like we only care whether it calls `force_shutdown` then, since a different test verifies the behavior of `force_shutdown` with regard to manipulating the signals. What I\u0027ve done in https://crrev.com/c/4800415/8 seems like a useful pattern for this, in that the test can mock out the board callbacks when they\u0027re unimportant while still being able to call the real implementation to test it.\n\nI hadn\u0027t looked at what exactly the code under test was doing, but I see now that the other test cases added in this CL do verify which signals are used as needed whereas this one doesn\u0027t actually care about signals at all.",
      "parentUuid": "8c052b76_e2dc8bc1",
      "revId": "a0d0ecb052df4ccf261b70932adcdce1cd70b48d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
