      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T21:36:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e For this particular one it seems like we only care whether it calls force_shutdown then, since a different test verifies the behavior of force_shutdown with regard to manipulating the signals.\n\nIn this test I am ensuring G3 entry function is called, since this calls `force_shutdown` I used this as my mechanism for ensuring this flow.\n\nBy providing AP Power sequence emulator I am ensuring the board specific code is bound to be called when moving into corresponding power state. \n\n\u003e What I\u0027ve done in https://crrev.com/c/4800415/8 seems like a useful pattern for this, in that the test can mock out the board callbacks when they\u0027re unimportant while still being able to call the real implementation to test it.\n\nWith `AP_PWRSEQ_DRIVER` every `board_ap_power_action_xxxx` function will not available (see CL:4079731). However, we can rely on AP Power sequence emulator to test all board functions by using driver API\u0027s to change power state and fit test requirements.",
      "parentUuid": "0390c050_ed13500b",
      "revId": "a0d0ecb052df4ccf261b70932adcdce1cd70b48d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f91fd4d2_ba5516ee",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/rex/tests/program/src/board_power.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 226,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-04T01:44:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It sounds like this is trying to test two things, then?\n\n1. `board_ap_power_action_g3_entry` is correctly registered with the subsystem and gets called on G3 entry\n2. the function sets signals to the expected G3 state\n \nIt\u0027s not clear to me that as currently written it really does either of those: it kind of does in that it expects some signals to be touched, but that could easily come from somewhere else.\n\nFor point 1 it would be ideal to instrument `board_ap_power_action_g3_entry` with a fake, but that seems difficult.\n\nFor point 2, there\u0027s already a test for `board_ap_power_force_shutdown` so we don\u0027t need to look at its behavior: mocking out `board_ap_power_force_shutdown` is sufficient to check that the handler calls that to set things to the expected state. Since we also know that this is the only thing `board_ap_power_action_g3_entry` does, mocking out `force_shutdown` also suffices to test that the handler was registered correctly.",
      "parentUuid": "43eae4ca_07f216f8",
      "revId": "a0d0ecb052df4ccf261b70932adcdce1cd70b48d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
